          "kicker": "Discipline warning",
          "heading": "Dallaglio warns Borthwick England's penalty count must fall before Australia",
          "body": "Lawrence Dallaglio splits England's penalty problem into pressure penalties, when they dominate the gainline, and execution penalties, when players pick the wrong option. He wants Steve Borthwick's side to show a noticeable difference, starting against Australia. The figures back his case: England have conceded 98 penalties in eight matches this year, an average of 12.25 a game, plus 14 yellow cards and one red. Against Argentina they gave away 15 penalties and four yellow cards, and still won 31-24."
