          "heading": "Franco Molina misses out as Tomás Lavanini returns for Ireland clash",
          "body": "Franco Molina, a mainstay of Felipe Contepomi's second-row selections since his 2024 debut, is not in the 33-man squad for the Ireland opener, the first November roster without him. Veteran Tomás Lavanini comes back in his place. Also omitted are veterans Matías Alemanno, Gonzalo Bertranou and Matías Moroni, the latter with 99 Test caps, while uncapped second-rower Luciano Asevedo, who has trained with the group this year, also misses out."
